Package: nexterm
Architecture: @ARCH@
Version: @VERSION@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: gnome-terminal (>= 3.44)
Description: browser surface inside an existing terminal
 NexTerm hosts a real WebKitGTK browser in a tab of your existing terminal
 (GNOME Terminal on X11): the page is rendered by an ordinary WebKit window
 which is reparented into the terminal window and follows its active tab.
 .
 It does not replace your terminal, does not intercept your shell, and does
 not take over your URL handler unless you run `nexterm handler enable`.
 .
 Environment: Linux + X11 + GNOME Terminal. Wayland is unsupported by design,
 and `nexterm doctor` reports that rather than failing obscurely.
